  "mathematical_review": {
    "count_policy_cone": "The complete84-count domain with one action and target per count defines the259-node ordered policy sigma(h)=s(count(h)). Induction identifies true prescribed and forced completions;504 comparisons,84 self-zero rows and deduplication of420 nonself rows give the same306-row63-type cone after positive scaling by12. This is a restricted complete-count record, not a general target-Markov purification theorem.",
    "single_client_value": "For the specified w47=1 point, all prescribed nonempty actions cover the sole client; any history with v prior coverers and r remaining gives every nonempty deviation1/(v+r), and emptyE gives0. ActualBCCC has u_i=1/4 and W=OPT4=1. A separate exact rational minimax/tangent saddle with uniform1/5 on the five nonempty labels proves t4=1/4; this source pays the static-value step, not full policy qualification or all15-record identity.",
    "rounding_and_floor_boundary": "Original binary q remains unnormalized and the final z47=1/4+2^-54 gives Fenchel lower bound1/4-2^-106. The positive debt upper bound alone is not a sign proof; exact zero comes from matching payoff/static bounds. The different Cartesian bank family refutes universal individual FF, while this one point has zero debt. No whole-cone FF, aggregate theorem or general/six-player half follows from this point.",
    "five_player_exact_optimum": "For the nine-type m5/p7 all-zero policy point, W1000 and the true last-node seven actions all pay200. The existing unanimous-terminal theorem gives OPT5<=1800; labels{0,1,2,4,5} attain1800. This is one exact optimum contribution to the finite construction, not proof of its full2801-node qualification or separate W3 recovery. The support independently explains the all-history inequalities.",
    "static_whole_theorem": "The algebraic frozen-deletion identity holds for any deterministic profile. An optimal indexed m-tuple, including repetitions, has average frozen total Q>=OPT_m-(1-1/m)W. The target static PNE inequalities averaged over all indices and summed over players pay W>=Q. Hence all static PNE satisfy OPT_m<=(2-1/m)W<=2W, including m1/W0, aliases, empty coverage and weak ties. This pays the whole registered static target.",
    "sequential_boundary": "General SPE IC controls a true continuation, not a frozen suffix. CAC has frozen4/3 versus true5/6; strict unique count-Markov DAA has root frozen13/3 versus true7/2. These refute a generic SPE-to-PNE bridge and do not refute the static theorem. Same-leaf/all-zero fixed-policy facts remain local. The support-only all127-type/all-J9/5 corollary is distinct from the old actual00055 fixed-J certificate and is not inserted into the finite-point target.",
    "peer_frozen_policy": "The pure-saddle sufficient condition certifies an auxiliary complete policy whose every action covers the same A, even when aliases vary by label history. The saved sigma differs only at212->5: the last player remains tied at3/2, and the only affected earlier IC at21 has slack1/3 reduced to0. At2 and the root all six true continuations avoid212; other prefixes cannot enter it. Thus this exact259-node sigma is SPE, actual3011 has each profit5/4,W5, and tuple(5,0,0,0) plus six total clients proves OPT4=6. The mature1554-row table is inherited evidence, not rerun. This is a whole fixed-construction implication, without a price optimum or unique/worst SPE claim.",
    "general_target_audit": "A supplemental independent3D audit and Root adoption review cover all46 accepted canonical Q-CAG-HALF incoming edges at matching current bytes/pins:23 whole are all conditional and23 are contributions. Alternative sufficient routes retain each internal ALL and common witness. The full-prefix RET antecedent is already refuted, so its valid implication is a dead counterfactual route, not a half refutation. Fixed populations, policies, structural classes, identities and local steps are not universal budgets. No new broken derivation or repair was identified. This semantic audit does not claim a fresh full audit of all mature source proofs.",
    "terminal_tax_preparation": "A separately saved read-only preparation reconstructs the fixed m4/p6 tax cone margin T/35 and the sharp welfare consequence OPT4<=7W/4. It compares the identical positive-depth policy in FREE230 and paid230, and distinguishes prefix tax, full terminal tax and ENT1. This preparation is not primary completion, does not clear its core pending state, and does not convert the welfare bound back into the stronger tax margin.",
